            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>
                    A gift to Isis. Gaius Papirius Macer Calventianus, son of Lucius, of tribe Poblilia, quattuorvir with aedilician power, quaestor of the treasury, flamen of Roma and Augustus. This place was given by decree of the decurions.
                </p>
